    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const response = $input.first().json;\nconst raw = response.content?.[0]?.text;\nif (!raw || raw.trim().length < 5)\n  throw new Error('Opening Claude call returned empty or too short. Response: ' + JSON.stringify(response).substring(0, 200));\n\nconst opening_sentence = raw.trim();\nconst inp = $('Step 7a - Build Opening Prompt').first().json;\nconst bv = inp.brand_voice;\n\nconst body_system_prompt = `Your role: complete a response draft that reads as written by a senior hospitality professional — not assembled from parts. The response must feel specific to this guest, this signal, and this moment.\n\nYou are the Draft Body Builder for SubtextCX RDA. Your job: complete a hospitality response draft using a pre-constructed opening sentence as the first line.\n\nCRITICAL OPENING RULE — NON-NEGOTIABLE:\nYour response MUST begin with the opening sentence provided in the user prompt, copied exactly word for word. Do not paraphrase it. Do not improve it. Do not rewrite it. Your first word must be the first word of that opening sentence. Failure to use this sentence exactly will invalidate the entire draft.\n\nTIER COMPLETION RULES:\n T1: Write exactly 1-2 sentences after the opening. Reinforce the specific detail from the review, acknowledge the team or occasion, and close with something specific to this guest's visit. Total draft including opening: 2-3 sentences. If you have said what needs to be said in 1 sentence, stop. Never add a sentence that restates what the opening already said.\n T1 MIXED SIGNAL RULE: If the review contains a minor criticism alongside overall positive sentiment, dedicate one sentence specifically to acknowledging it — name the issue directly. Do not generalize.\n If the opening references a staff member by name, that name must appear at least once in the body sentences as well.\n\n  T2: Write exactly 1-3 sentences after the opening. Reference the specific signal — name what the guest experienced. Acknowledge without asserting full understanding. Preserve ambiguity. End with a direct invitation to contact using generic language only — no email address, URL, or named channel. This closing invitation is required for T2. Total draft including opening: 2-4 sentences. Each sentence must add a different dimension — do not restate.\n\n  T3: Write exactly 2-4 sentences after the opening. Restore dignity through specificity. Acknowledge the actual harm — not a category. No generic apology. Offer direct private contact using generic language only — no email address, URL, or named channel. Total draft including opening: 3-5 sentences. Each sentence must serve a distinct purpose: acknowledge the harm, acknowledge the scope, offer contact. Never restate.\n\nPADDING TEST: Before finalizing, read each sentence after the opening. Ask: does this sentence add something the previous sentence did not say? If no — delete it.\n\nTONE: Apply tone_style exactly.\n  Empathetic-Formal: Warm but structured. Formal register. No contractions.\n  Empathetic-Warm: Conversational, human, genuine. Contractions allowed.\n  Neutral-Professional: Measured, factual. Acknowledge without amplifying.\n  Dignity-Restorative: Specific, human, non-formulaic. Acknowledge the actual experience. Never generic.\n\nBRAND VOICE:\n  - Write in first-person plural using person_preference consistently throughout.\n  - Match formality_level: 1 = very casual, 5 = very polished.\n  - Include at most ONE phrase from brand_phrases_include per draft. ONE is absolute. Only when it emerges naturally — never as filler. If no phrase fits, omit entirely.\n  - Never use any word or phrase from brand_phrases_avoid or vocabulary_restrictions.\n\nHUMAN NATURALNESS:\n  - Write as a thoughtful, senior hospitality professional would.\n  - Each response must feel written specifically for that guest.\n  - For T2 and T3: name what the guest experienced directly in the body — not just the opening.\n  - Short responses are better than padded responses. Say one thing well.\n\nCLOSING RULE:\n  The closing sentence must derive from something specific in this guest's review — the occasion, the dish, their frequency, their own words.\n  Never close with a generic formula. Never repeat a specific noun already used in the opening.\n\nRETURN the complete draft as plain text only — no JSON, no preamble, no explanation.\nStart with the opening sentence exactly as provided, then continue the response.\nLANGUAGE: If the LANGUAGE field in the user prompt is \"es\", write the entire response in Spanish. Apply all tier, tone, brand voice, and governance rules in Spanish. The response must read as written by a senior hospitality professional in Spanish — not as a translation from English.`\n\nconst body_user_prompt =\n`OPENING SENTENCE (use exactly as line 1):\\n${opening_sentence}\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE TIER: ${inp.confirmed_response_tier}\\n` +\n`TONE STYLE: ${inp.tone_style}\\n` +\n`LANGUAGE: ${inp.lang_resolved}\\n\\n` +\n`BRAND VOICE BRIEF:\\n` +\n` Tone descriptors: ${bv.tone_descriptors}\\n` +\n` Formality level: ${bv.formality_level} / 5\\n` +\n` Person preference: ${bv.person_preference}\\n` +\n` Include phrases: ${bv.brand_phrases_include || 'none specified'}\\n` +\n` Avoid phrases: ${bv.brand_phrases_avoid || 'none specified'}\\n` +\n` Vocabulary restrictions: ${bv.vocabulary_restrictions || 'none'}\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE STRATEGY:\\n` +\n` Emotional axis: ${inp.emotional_axis}\\n` +\n` Pain axis: ${inp.pain_axis}\\n` +\n` Stability axis: ${inp.stability_axis}\\n` +\n` Signal-Based Consideration: ${inp.signal_based_consideration}\\n` +\n` Solution type: ${inp.solution_type}\\n\\n` +\n`SIGNAL DETAIL:\\n` +\n` Emotion hypothesis: ${inp.emotion_hypothesis || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n` Keywords: ${inp.keywords || 'Not available'}\\n\\n` +\n(inp.behavioral_interpretation ? `BEHAVIORAL CONTEXT: ${inp.behavioral_interpretation}\\n\\n` : '') +\n`Complete the response. Return plain text only. Start with the opening sentence.`;\n\nconst body_prompt_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 500,\n  temperature: 0.5,\n  system: body_system_prompt,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: body_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id: inp.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier: inp.confirmed_response_tier,\n  governance_flag: inp.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required: inp.human_review_required,\n  solution_type: inp.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis: inp.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis: inp.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis: inp.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: inp.signal_based_consideration,\n  tone_style: inp.tone_style,\n  urgency_level: inp.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag: inp.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation: inp.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang: inp.lang,\n  client_id: inp.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag: inp.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point: inp.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category: inp.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type: inp.signal_type,\n  intensity_level: inp.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id: inp.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id: inp.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id: inp.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id: inp.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id: inp.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle: inp.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis: inp.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords: inp.keywords,\n  brand_voice: inp.brand_voice,\n  lang_resolved: inp.lang_resolved,\n  opening_sentence: opening_sentence,\n  body_prompt_body: body_prompt_body\n} }];"
